  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `node_content` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Contents]/fn[node_content]` is appropriate.\n\n- **Form:** The citation sits on an explicitly declared function with a body. Its fenced commentary gives a substantive reason, not just difficulty. The test only inspects `outgoing_edges` and asserts `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` records, so no content read is wanted. The `panic!` body is a guard that fails the test if contents are ever read.\n- **Agreement with the source:** The `Contents` trait in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs` requires `node_content`, `fingerprint` and `format_node_content`. `Domain` and `InspectionContext<D: Contents>` also bound on `Contents`. So the test graph must supply the callback even though the test must not call it. This matches the commentary's claim that \"Contents requires this callback\".\n- **Test behavior:** The test's assertions match the commentary. The recorded dependencies are only `OutgoingEdges`, and the test asserts the exact dependency list. No node content, fingerprint or formatting dependency is ever expected.\n- **Other references:** The item carries no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same target, so nothing is redundant.",
